WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.379
The render subsystem covers the engine's lifecycle, what happens in

00:00:07.479 --> 00:00:12.129
each frame, culling, batching, effects, and the transform hierarchy.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:18.696
WasmGPU.create takes a canvas and a descriptor: antialiasing,

00:00:18.796 --> 00:00:23.538
power preference, canvas format, frustum and occlusion culling

00:00:23.638 --> 00:00:26.349
with their stats, and device limits.

00:00:26.766 --> 00:00:30.595
warmup prebuilds pipelines and other render resources for a

00:00:30.695 --> 00:00:33.792
scene and camera before the first visible frame.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.937
run starts the loop and stop ends it, isRunning reports

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:42.612
the state, render draws one frame, and destroy releases everything.

00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:48.644
Each render call updates camera matrices and dirty transforms,

00:00:48.744 --> 00:00:51.836
then builds a draw list for each object family.

00:00:52.266 --> 00:00:57.113
It prepares shadows and packs model matrices, filters and sorts what is

00:00:57.213 --> 00:01:01.852
visible, encodes the passes, and submits them in one command buffer.

00:01:02.266 --> 00:01:06.778
You control the inputs, the scene, camera, descriptor, and effects, and

00:01:06.878 --> 00:01:10.806
the stats panel and culling counters show what each frame did.

00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:17.784
Frustum culling tests each object's world-space bounding sphere against the

00:01:17.884 --> 00:01:21.081
six camera planes in Rust, and is on by default.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.648
Occlusion culling is opt-in: it reuses a low-resolution depth hierarchy from

00:01:26.748 --> 00:01:30.722
the previous frame to skip opaque objects that were hidden.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:35.165
It is conservative, it is skipped unless the viewport, camera, and

00:01:35.265 --> 00:01:39.673
occluders still match the captured hierarchy, and picking never uses it.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.499
cullingStats reports how many objects

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:44.864
were tested, visible, and occluded.

00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:51.010
Consecutive opaque meshes that share a pipeline, material,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.305
and geometry are drawn as one instanced run,

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:57.525
and unchanged runs reuse their packed data.

00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:01.777
Transparent objects from all six families are merged into

00:02:01.877 --> 00:02:05.790
one back-to-front order, without building a combined list.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.422
Gaussian splats and transparent 3D lattice cells are sorted

00:02:10.522 --> 00:02:13.353
per element on the GPU with radix sorts.

00:02:15.266 --> 00:02:21.347
Shadows are enabled per directional light through effects.shadows, with

00:02:21.447 --> 00:02:25.961
a 1024-pixel map and 3-by-3 PCF filtering by default.

00:02:26.366 --> 00:02:30.456
Hard filtering and manual updates are available, and each shadow

00:02:30.556 --> 00:02:33.861
view fits an orthographic box to the camera frustum.

00:02:34.266 --> 00:02:38.686
Meshes cast shadows with castShadow, and only standard materials

00:02:38.786 --> 00:02:43.276
receive them; the scientific primitives neither cast nor receive.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.841
Antialiasing is optional subpixel morphological

00:02:47.941 --> 00:02:51.450
antialiasing, SMAA, enabled at creation.

00:02:53.366 --> 00:02:59.090
createPerformanceStats adds a panel with frame rate, CPU and GPU timing,

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:04.509
and culling counters, with GPU timing when timestamp queries exist.

00:03:04.933 --> 00:03:09.973
createTransform adds a node to the structure-of-arrays transform store, with

00:03:10.073 --> 00:03:13.964
parenting that rejects cycles and pointers to its matrices.

00:03:14.366 --> 00:03:19.012
Changes mark nodes dirty, and Rust recomposes local matrices and

00:03:19.112 --> 00:03:23.461
multiplies each world matrix by its parent's before drawing.

00:03:25.366 --> 00:03:29.171
To recap: the engine lifecycle, the per-frame stages,

00:03:29.271 --> 00:03:33.001
two kinds of culling, batching and ordering, shadows

00:03:33.101 --> 00:03:35.506
and SMAA, and the transform store.

00:03:36.933 --> 00:03:40.844
The full reference is in the Render section of the documentation.
